# Normalize line endings repo-wide: git stores LF; Windows working tree gets CRLF via core.autocrlf.
# Added 2026-07-12 to end perpetual phantom-modified flags from pre-existing CRLF blobs.
* text=auto

# E11 (2026-11-08): files with a `#!` shebang must keep LF in the working tree too. With
# `* text=auto` + core.autocrlf a Windows checkout rewrites `#!/usr/bin/env node\n` to `...\r\n`,
# and Node's ESM loader then throws "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" on import (this broke
# tests/scripts/check-migrations-applied.test.ts on Windows); bash likewise rejects CRLF scripts.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
